  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1053 PM CDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nDewpoints are expected to be a bit higher on Saturday as winds\nturn around to the south, but not high enough to raise forecast\nheat indices to advisory levels. Deterministic and ensemble data\ncontinues to support the ridge center aloft shifting overhead this\nweekend, then over to the mid-Mississippi and Ohio Valleys early\nnext week and then back overhead late next week into next weekend.\nAt the surface, a trough will be situated to our north and west\nand the gradient will tighten over the region, bringing breezy\nconditions late in the weekend and into next week. The ridge \naloft will maintain above average heat and dry weather over the \nregion at least through next week. Heat headlines may be needed as\nsoon as Sunday and for several days next week for portions of the\narea. The 18Z GFS total QPF forecast was basically zero over the \nforecast area through the first week of September. Drought \nconditions over the region will worsen. The hot, dry and windy \nconditions will increase fire weather concerns at least locally \neach day.\n\nThe week 2 forecast from the CPC suggests continued support for\nabove average temps and below average precip until further notice.\n\nLacy",
